  Two rounded screens, the controller you hold and the taller companion display, with a
  relay wedge carrying content between them.

  Every coordinate sits inside the 66dp safe circle centred on (54, 54), so no launcher
  mask (circle, squircle, rounded square, teardrop) clips anything. That is asserted, not
  assumed: running branding/generate_launcher_icons.py with the check flag fails if any
  extreme point leaves the circle.

  Generated from that same script, the single source of truth shared with
  branding/relay-display-logo.svg. Do not hand edit these paths; change the script and
  re-run it, or the two copies will disagree.
-->
